  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What it works out",
      "items": [
        "approximation[n] = sum over k of x[2n + k] * low[k]",
        "detail[n] = sum over k of x[2n + k] * high[k]",
        "Each holds half the samples, thus the two together hold as many as went in"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "How the library gets there",
      "items": [
        "The two filters are one filter and its mirror",
        "The mirror is what makes the pair undoable at all",
        "dwt_inverse puts the samples back between the answers and runs them the other way"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "What it is for",
      "items": [
        "A Fourier transform says which frequencies, and not where they are",
        "Each detail belongs to one place, thus a step shows as a few large details",
        "Noise spreads thinly over every detail, and an edge does not"
      ]
